  "lineage": "Saltarello central-and-southern Italian folk-dance-and-music tradition of Lazio, Abruzzo, Marche, and Molise regions, characterized by fast triple-meter or 6/8 leaping-dance with characteristic accelerating tempo. Origin documented in fourteenth-century Italian musical manuscripts (the Saltarello primo and secondo in the Add MS 29987 British Library manuscript) and preserved in continuous folk-tradition through the medieval-Renaissance-modern transition. Performance: tambourine-led ensemble with accordion, fiddle, organetto button-accordion, and chorus. Distinguished from tarantella by saltarello's central-Italian regional base and characteristic standing-leap (vs spinning) choreographic register. The post-1970s Italian-folk-revival reactivated the genre in the original regional contexts.",
